:false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T13:19:51Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T13:19:51Z","body":"**Software report:**\n\n```\ngithub.com/AlDanial/cloc v 1.98  T=0.11 s (879.3 files/s, 153370.5 lines/s)\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLanguage                     files          blank        comment           code\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPython                          58           1872           5027           7645\nMarkdown                        22            257              0            785\nYAML                             8             78              8            441\nTOML                             5             25              0            437\nTeX                              1             18              0            285\nCSV                              2              0              0            223\nmake                             1             39              7            105\nJavaScript                       1              0              0             10\nCSS                              1              1              0              5\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSUM:                            99           2290           5042           9936\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n```\n\n**Commit count by author**:\n\n```\n   294\tgtrevisan\n   246\tJoshua Lorincz\n   232\thturner08\n    98\tGregorio L. Trevisan\n    43\tJosh Lorincz\n    38\tamdecker\n    36\t+Herbert Turner\n    33\tWilliam Wei\n    32\tandrew-maris\n    26\tZanderKeith\n    13\tAmos Decker\n     8\tcrea-psfc\n     6\tAlex R. Saperstein\n     3\tyumouwei\n     2\tAllen Wang\n     1\t+Joshua Lorincz\n     1\tCristina Rea\n     1\tHenry Wietfeldt\n```\n\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497234762/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497235120","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497235120","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497235120,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qc5Kw","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T13:19:57Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T13:19:57Z","body":"**Paper file info**:\n\n📄 Wordcount for `paper.md` is **466**\n\n✅ The paper includes a `Statement of need` section\n\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497235120/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497235271","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497235271","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497235271,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qc5NH","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T13:20:00Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T13:20:00Z","body":"**License info**:\n\n✅ License found: `MIT License` (Valid open source [OSI approved](https://opensource.org/licenses) license)\n\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497235271/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497237793","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497237793","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497237793,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qc50h","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T13:20:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T14:16:17Z","body":"Hi  @gtrevisan, @LiamPattinson, @jackleland, @rmrsk this is the review thread for the paper.\nAll of our communications will happen here from now on.\n\nAs a reviewer, the first step is to create a checklist for your review by entering\n```\n@editorialbot generate my checklist\n```\nas the top of a new comment in this thread.\n\nThese checklists contain the JOSS requirements.\nAs you go over the submission, please check off anything that you feel has been satisfied for publication in JOSS. The first comment in this thread also contains links to the [JOSS reviewer guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/reviewer_guidelines.html).\n\nThe JOSS review is different from some other journals. Our goal is to work with the authors to help them meet our criteria instead of merely passing judgment on the submission. As such, the reviewers are encouraged to submit issues and pull requests on the software repository. When doing so, please mention `openjournals/joss-reviews#9364` so that a link is created to this thread. Please also feel free to comment and ask questions on this thread. You are welcome to post comments/questions/suggestions as you come across them instead of waiting until you've reviewed the entire package.\n\nWe aim for reviews to be completed within about 2-4 weeks. Please let me know if any of you require some more time.\nWe can also use EditorialBot (our bot) to set automatic reminders if you know you'll be away for a known period of time.\nI'll check back in in a fortnight to see how things are progressing.\n\nPlease feel free to ping me (@jatkinson1000) if you have any questions/concerns.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497237793/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497239570","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497239570","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497239570,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qc6QS","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T13:21:09Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T13:21:09Z","body":":point_right::page_facing_up: [Download article proof](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openjournals/joss-papers/joss.09364/joss.09364/10.21105.joss.09364.pdf) :page_facing_up: [View article proof on GitHub](https://github.com/openjournals/joss-papers/blob/joss.09364/joss.09364/10.21105.joss.09364.pdf) :page_facing_up: :point_left:","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497239570/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497239933","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497239933","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497239933,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qc6V9","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T13:21:14Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T13:21:14Z","body":"@editorialbot remind me in 14 days","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497239933/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497240102","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497240102","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497240102,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qc6Ym","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T13:21:17Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T13:21:17Z","body":"Reminder set for @jatkinson1000 in 14 days","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497240102/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497389779","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497389779","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497389779,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qde7T","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T13:57:22Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T13:57:55Z","body":"Hi all, thanks for helping out with our submission!\n\nI am planning to release [v0.12](https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/pull/455) in the next few days, ahead of our [yearly APS-DPP meeting](https://engage.aps.org/dpp/meetings/annual-meeting), thus I will soon merge the current `dev` branch onto `main`, and I will branch off a new development branch for v0.13.\nDue to timing alone, I imagine any proposed feature or bugfix would happen as a new PR onto v0.13-dev.\n\n@jatkinson1000 Please let me know whether JOSS requires any specific development cycle, or enforces any other rule or logic (with impact to our current release workflow) that I should be aware of.\n\nAllow me then to quote [my own comment from the pre-review thread](https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/8538#issuecomment-3427021571) for our reviewers' benefit:\n\n> ### Alcator C-Mod\n> \n> In order to access data for [Alcator C-Mod](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcator_C-Mod) (MIT's own now-decommissioned machine, prototypical for these workflows) one has to _request access_ -- any reviewer might do that easily, and I would make sure any request is pushed forward in a timely fashion. That's because the [MDSplus server](https://www.mdsplus.org/) hosting our C-Mod data is not public-facing and does require authentication and computer access on our [MIT PSFC](https://www.psfc.mit.edu/) systems.\n> ### MAST\n> \n> We currently have UKAEA collaborators helping out and implementing physics methods for [MAST data, which is open access](https://mastapp.site/). Since the S3 endpoints hosting MAST experimental data as Zarr-backed Xarrays are world-readable, anybody can try out our MAST workflows at any time, anywhere.\n> \n> (Other machines have more stringent requirements for accessing data.)\n> \n> The framework code is shared among all devices, and only the physics methods will be machine-specific. All these methods are open-source so as to allow anybody to take a look at our physics workflows, but they will pull data from the appropriate authorized sources.\n> \n> I guess it depends on what level of detail each reviewer might deem appropriate to test our code -- I believe the MAST proof-of-concept might be enough for most purposes but, if not, C-Mod access will be granted easily. How would you like to proceed?\n\nThank you all!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497389779/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497412913","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497412913","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497412913,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qdkkx","user":{"login":"LiamPattinson","id":14332134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMyMTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14332134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson","html_url":"https://github.com/LiamPattinson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T14:03:28Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T12:35:43Z","body":"## Review checklist for @LiamPattinson\n\n### Conflict of interest\n\n- [x] I confirm that I have read the [JOSS conflict of interest (COI) policy](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/COI.md) and that: I have no COIs with reviewing this work or that any perceived COIs have been waived by JOSS for the purpose of this review.\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [x] I confirm that I read and will adhere to the [JOSS code of conduct](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).\n\n### General checks\n\n- [x] **Repository:** Is the source code for this software available at the [https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py](https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py)?\n- [x] **License:** Does the repository contain a plain-text LICENSE or COPYING file with the contents of an [OSI approved](https://opensource.org/licenses/alphabetical) software license?\n- [x] **Contribution and authorship:** Has the submitting author (@gtrevisan) made major contributions to the software? Does the full list of paper authors seem appropriate and complete?\n- [x] **Substantial scholarly effort:** Does this submission meet the scope eligibility described in the [JOSS guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/submitting.html#substantial-scholarly-effort)\n- [x] **Data sharing:** If the paper contains original data, data are accessible to the reviewers. If the paper contains no original data, please check this item.\n- [x] **Reproducibility:** If the paper contains original results, results are entirely reproducible by reviewers. If the paper contains no original results, please check this item.\n- [x] **Human and animal research:** If the paper contains original data research on humans subjects or animals, does it comply with [JOSS's human participants research policy and/or animal research policy](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/policies.html?highlight=animal#joss-policies)? If the paper contains no such data, please check this item.\n\n\n### Functionality\n\n- [x] **Installation:** Does installation proceed as outlined in the documentation?\n- [x] **Functionality:** Have the functional claims of the software been confirmed?\n- [x] **Performance:** If there are any performance claims of the software, have they been confirmed? (If there are no claims, please check off this item.)\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [x] **A statement of need**: Do the authors clearly state what problems the software is designed to solve and who the target audience is?\n- [x] **Installation instructions:** Is there a clearly-stated list of dependencies? Ideally these should be handled with an automated package management solution.\n- [x] **Example usage:** Do the authors include examples of how to use the software (ideally to solve real-world analysis problems).\n- [x] **Functionality documentation:** Is the core functionality of the software documented to a satisfactory level (e.g., API method documentation)?\n- [x] **Automated tests:** Are there automated tests or manual steps described so that the functionality of the software can be verified?\n- [x] **Community guidelines:** Are there clear guidelines for third parties wishing to 1. Contribute to the software 2. Report issues or problems with the software 3. Seek support\n\n### Software paper\n\n- [x] **Summary:** Has a clear description of the high-level functionality and purpose of the software for a diverse, non-specialist audience been provided?\n- [x] **A statement of need:** Does the paper have a section titled 'Statement of need' that clearly states what problems the software is designed to solve, who the target audience is, and its relation to other work?\n- [x] **State of the field:** Do the authors describe how this software compares to other commonly-used packages?\n- [x] **Quality of writing:** Is the paper well written (i.e., it does not require editing for structure, language, or writing quality)?\n- [x] **References:** Is the list of references complete, and is everything cited appropriately that should be cited (e.g., papers, datasets, software)? Do references in the text use the proper [citation syntax](https://pandoc.org/MANUAL.html#extension-citations)?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497412913/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497426400","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497426400","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497426400,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qdn3g","user":{"login":"LiamPattinson","id":14332134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMyMTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14332134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson","html_url":"https://github.com/LiamPattinson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T14:06:59Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T14:06:59Z","body":"I'll be (extremely) busy until November 17th, and will be able to start my review then. Apologies for not bringing this up in the previous thread, I hope it won't be an issue! In the meantime, please let me know if I need to provide any details in order to gain access to the MDSplus server.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497426400/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497446641","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497446641","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497446641,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qdszx","user":{"login":"jackleland","id":25505076,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NTA1MDc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25505076?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackleland","html_url":"https://github.com/jackleland","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackleland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackleland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackleland/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackleland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackleland/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackleland/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackleland/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackleland/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackleland/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T14:11:34Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T11:15:03Z","body":"## Review checklist for @jackleland\n\n### Conflict of interest\n\n- [x] I confirm that I have read the [JOSS conflict of interest (COI) policy](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/COI.md) and that: I have no COIs with reviewing this work or that any perceived COIs have been waived by JOSS for the purpose of this review.\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [x] I confirm that I read and will adhere to the [JOSS code of conduct](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).\n\n### General checks\n\n- [x] **Repository:** Is the source code for this software available at the [https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py](https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py)?\n- [x] **License:** Does the repository contain a plain-text LICENSE or COPYING file with the contents of an [OSI approved](https://opensource.org/licenses/alphabetical) software license?\n- [x] **Contribution and authorship:** Has the submitting author (@gtrevisan) made major contributions to the software? Does the full list of paper authors seem appropriate and complete?\n- [x] **Substantial scholarly effort:** Does this submission meet the scope eligibility described in the [JOSS guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/submitting.html#substantial-scholarly-effort)\n- [x] **Data sharing:** If the paper contains original data, data are accessible to the reviewers. If the paper contains no original data, please check this item.\n- [x] **Reproducibility:** If the paper contains original results, results are entirely reproducible by reviewers. If the paper contains no original results, please check this item.\n- [x] **Human and animal research:** If the paper contains original data research on humans subjects or animals, does it comply with [JOSS's human participants research policy and/or animal research policy](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/policies.html?highlight=animal#joss-policies)? If the paper contains no such data, please check this item.\n\n\n### Functionality\n\n- [x] **Installation:** Does installation proceed as outlined in the documentation?\n- [x] **Functionality:** Have the functional claims of the software been confirmed?\n- [x] **Performance:** If there are any performance claims of the software, have they been confirmed? (If there are no claims, please check off this item.)\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [x] **A statement of need**: Do the authors clearly state what problems the software is designed to solve and who the target audience is?\n- [x] **Installation instructions:** Is there a clearly-stated list of dependencies? Ideally these should be handled with an automated package management solution.\n- [x] **Example usage:** Do the authors include examples of how to use the software (ideally to solve real-world analysis problems).\n- [x] **Functionality documentation:** Is the core functionality of the software documented to a satisfactory level (e.g., API method documentation)?\n- [x] **Automated tests:** Are there automated tests or manual steps described so that the functionality of the software can be verified?\n- [x] **Community guidelines:** Are there clear guidelines for third parties wishing to 1. Contribute to the software 2. Report issues or problems with the software 3. Seek support\n\n### Software paper\n\n- [x] **Summary:** Has a clear description of the high-level functionality and purpose of the software for a diverse, non-specialist audience been provided?\n- [x] **A statement of need:** Does the paper have a section titled 'Statement of need' that clearly states what problems the software is designed to solve, who the target audience is, and its relation to other work?\n- [x] **State of the field:** Do the authors describe how this software compares to other commonly-used packages?\n- [x] **Quality of writing:** Is the paper well written (i.e., it does not require editing for structure, language, or writing quality)?\n- [x] **References:** Is the list of references complete, and is everything cited appropriately that should be cited (e.g., papers, datasets, software)? Do references in the text use the proper [citation syntax](https://pandoc.org/MANUAL.html#extension-citations)?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497446641/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497474843","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497474843","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497474843,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Qdzsb","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T14:18:28Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T19:55:48Z","body":"## Review checklist for @rmrsk\n\n### Conflict of interest\n\n- [x] I confirm that I have read the [JOSS conflict of interest (COI) policy](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/COI.md) and that: I have no COIs with reviewing this work or that any perceived COIs have been waived by JOSS for the purpose of this review.\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [x] I confirm that I read and will adhere to the [JOSS code of conduct](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).\n\n### General checks\n\n- [x] **Repository:** Is the source code for this software available at the [https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py](https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py)?\n- [x] **License:** Does the repository contain a plain-text LICENSE or COPYING file with the contents of an [OSI approved](https://opensource.org/licenses/alphabetical) software license?\n- [x] **Contribution and authorship:** Has the submitting author (@gtrevisan) made major contributions to the software? Does the full list of paper authors seem appropriate and complete?\n- [x] **Substantial scholarly effort:** Does this submission meet the scope eligibility described in the [JOSS guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/submitting.html#substantial-scholarly-effort)\n- [x] **Data sharing:** If the paper contains original data, data are accessible to the reviewers. If the paper contains no original data, please check this item.\n- [x] **Reproducibility:** If the paper contains original results, results are entirely reproducible by reviewers. If the paper contains no original results, please check this item.\n- [x] **Human and animal research:** If the paper contains original data research on humans subjects or animals, does it comply with [JOSS's human participants research policy and/or animal research policy](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/policies.html?highlight=animal#joss-policies)? If the paper contains no such data, please check this item.\n\n\n### Functionality\n\n- [x] **Installation:** Does installation proceed as outlined in the documentation?\n- [x] **Functionality:** Have the functional claims of the software been confirmed?\n- [x] **Performance:** If there are any performance claims of the software, have they been confirmed? (If there are no claims, please check off this item.)\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [x] **A statement of need**: Do the authors clearly state what problems the software is designed to solve and who the target audience is?\n- [x] **Installation instructions:** Is there a clearly-stated list of dependencies? Ideally these should be handled with an automated package management solution.\n- [x] **Example usage:** Do the authors include examples of how to use the software (ideally to solve real-world analysis problems).\n- [x] **Functionality documentation:** Is the core functionality of the software documented to a satisfactory level (e.g., API method documentation)?\n- [x] **Automated tests:** Are there automated tests or manual steps described so that the functionality of the software can be verified?\n- [x] **Community guidelines:** Are there clear guidelines for third parties wishing to 1. Contribute to the software 2. Report issues or problems with the software 3. Seek support\n\n### Software paper\n\n- [x] **Summary:** Has a clear description of the high-level functionality and purpose of the software for a diverse, non-specialist audience been provided?\n- [x] **A statement of need:** Does the paper have a section titled 'Statement of need' that clearly states what problems the software is designed to solve, who the target audience is, and its relation to other work?\n- [x] **State of the field:** Do the authors describe how this software compares to other commonly-used packages?\n- [x] **Quality of writing:** Is the paper well written (i.e., it does not require editing for structure, language, or writing quality)?\n- [x] **References:** Is the list of references complete, and is everything cited appropriately that should be cited (e.g., papers, datasets, software)? Do references in the text use the proper [citation syntax](https://pandoc.org/MANUAL.html#extension-citations)?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497474843/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497531561","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3497531561","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3497531561,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7QeBip","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T14:31:56Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T14:31:56Z","body":"@LiamPattinson @jackleland @rmrsk\n\nYou may request an account on our systems [from this webpage](https://account.psfc.mit.edu/).\nI'd choose:\n- Position Type/Affiliation = Collaborator/s\n- Supervisor = myself\n- Job Description = testing of the disruption-py workflow with C-mod data for publication review\n- Account type = Windows and Linux\n\nYou are also free to test out the non-authwalled [MAST workflow](https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/commits/slj/mast/) -- that workflow is the first to rely on Xarray, rather than MDSplus, and as such is still very much under active development.\nWe will enlist UKAEA's own @samueljackson92 if needed. 🙃","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3497531561/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3501884990","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3501884990","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3501884990,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7QuoY-","user":{"login":"LiamPattinson","id":14332134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMyMTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14332134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson","html_url":"https://github.com/LiamPattinson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T11:00:08Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T11:00:08Z","body":"Thanks @gtrevisan. The page you linked contains the following note:\n\n> NOTE: IF YOU ARE A COLLABORATOR, VISITING SCIENTIST, OR VISITING STUDENT,WE MUST HAVE SIGNED COLLABORATION AGREEMENT WITH YOU, BEFORE YOU SUBMIT THIS ACCOUNT REQUEST. OTHERWISE, THIS REQUEST WILL BE DENIED. IF YOU DON'T KNOW WHAT THIS IS, ASK YOUR SUPERVISOR.\n\nWill that be an issue for the application? If you need to send any paperwork to me, you can do so at liam.pattinson@york.ac.uk","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3501884990/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3502038581","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3502038581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3502038581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7QvN41","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T11:32:59Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T11:32:59Z","body":"@gtrevisan JOSS is particular about the software version linked to publication being the same as the one that was reviewed.\n\nAs such I'd suggest making the reviewers aware of any code that you want to appear in the review process provided it isn't scattered across many branches and will be merged soon.\nIt may also be that you make some improvements as a result of the review that require merging into a minor/patch version for the final publication.\n\nWhat you described above seems consistent with this approach.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3502038581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3503083962","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3503083962","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3503083962,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7QzNG6","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T15:06:47Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T15:06:47Z","body":"Due to our yearly conference and all the efforts going into it, no development will happen in the next few weeks.\nI will still merge our `dev` branch onto `main`, possibly later today, in order to avoid any confusion for reviewers.\nThe officially-reviewed version will then be `v0.12`.\n\n@LiamPattinson you can go ahead and submit an account request.\nI will work on further documentation in parallel to that.\n\nOnce again, it really depends on the level of detail at which you'd like to conduct your review -- that's required only for C-mod data access.\nA quick no-prerequisites workflow should work if running from the MAST development branch, `slj/mast`:\n\n```bash\n# eg: I love uv for such fast on-the-fly workflows\n[user@host: ~] uvx --from git+https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py@slj/mast disruption-py\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3503083962/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3503603121","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3503603121","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3503603121,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Q1L2x","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T16:44:55Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T16:44:55Z","body":"@LiamPattinson @jackleland @rmrsk\nIf you wish to access Alcator C-Mod data, please read and sign [this Data Agreement](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YgOJ2mG1syN8U_lAcsR3CnttHA29ySUC) and return it to me via email -- I will then countersign it and collect our Division Head's approval.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3503603121/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3503719782","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3503719782","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3503719782,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Q1oVm","user":{"login":"kyleniemeyer","id":190432,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MDQzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190432?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer","html_url":"https://github.com/kyleniemeyer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T17:09:04Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T17:09:04Z","body":"Just jumping in here as the track AEiC: software that requires approval for reviewing, collaborating, or accessing data/code is *not* compatible with JOSS.\n\nReviewers should not be signing anything. If running or testing the code requires some private data, then the software is not suitable for publication in JOSS.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3503719782/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3503891053","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3503891053","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3503891053,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Q2SJt","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T17:43:59Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T17:43:59Z","body":"Thanks @kyleniemeyer I was just trying to check this.\nMy understanding - and I hope @gtrevisan can confirm - is that there is MAST data freely available to test the library with, and this discussion covers additional datasets with other permissions?\n\nWhilst it is not uncommon for data providers to require an account to download data to reduce spamming (e.g. USGS, JAXA, Copernicus Climate Data) these are all simple and automated registration processes. If something requires wet signatures and manual approval then this is not in the spirit of open community software.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3503891053/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3504235127","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3504235127","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3504235127,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Q3mJ3","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T18:46:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T14:16:22Z","body":"MAST data is [open access](https://mastapp.site/).\nAccess for the other machines (eg Alcator C-Mod) requires some kind of acknowledgement/authorization in order to make sure that collaborators follow the proper scientific channels (eg: before disseminating previously-unpublished results).\n\nData coming from ([_very_ expensive](https://www.cfs.energy/news-and-media/commonwealth-fusion-systems-raises-863-million-series-b2-round-to-accelerate-the-commercialization-of-fusion-energy)) fusion devices is often kept under stricter control for even longer, but thankfully that is not our case as [Alcator C-Mod](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcator_C-Mod) stopped operating almost 10y ago.\nAnybody can be granted access to it freely, all the more if it was publicly-funded research in the first place (eg: [DOE FES](https://www.energy.gov/science/fes/fusion-energy-sciences)).\nIt is true that our authorization process is clunky, but I don't see whether this should be any different than, say, having a series of [very complicated checkboxes with EULA terms written in tiny font](https://www.huffpost.com/entry/gamestation-grabs-souls-o_n_541549) on a streamlined webpage.\n\nFurthermore, there is a huge difference between open _software_ and open _data_ -- when I submitted in July I did my best to read through all FAQs and I missed any reference to [openness](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/submitting.html#:~:text=open) of data.\n\nFinally, allow me to mention once again that almost all parts of the framework will be invoked even by our MAST workflow, from the user configuration and settings, to the complicated portions of multiprocessing and physics method caching and invocation, through timebase interpolations and up to final output.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3504235127/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3504427904","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3504427904","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3504427904,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Q4VOA","user":{"login":"kyleniemeyer","id":190432,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MDQzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190432?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer","html_url":"https://github.com/kyleniemeyer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyleniemeyer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T19:19:07Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T19:19:07Z","body":"@gtrevisan I'm not quite sure what you are getting at with this reference:\n> It is true that our authorization process is clunky, but I don't see whether this should be any different than, say, having a series of [very complicated checkboxes with EULA terms written in tiny font](https://www.huffpost.com/entry/gamestation-grabs-souls-o_n_541549) on a streamlined webpage.\n\nJOSS would not publish something that requires such an onerous process. We aren't saying that your code / approach is not ethically or legally permissible in the world, but JOSS has specific requirements. Some of those are that reviewers (like any user) must be able to access both the code—including any data needed to test the code—\"without manual approval of (or payment for) accounts\".","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3504427904/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3510099117","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3510099117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3510099117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7RN9yt","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T08:21:26Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T08:21:26Z","body":"@kyleniemeyer How should I deal with this? Should I proceed with the review or not? ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3510099117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3510142661","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3510142661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3510142661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7ROIbF","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T08:31:00Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T08:31:00Z","body":"@gtrevisan Now we've had the weekend to pause, please could you confirm if functionalities of your software package can be fully tested and evaluated using the [open source MAST dataset](https://mastapp.site/) that is freely available to reviewers without any contractual agreements?\n\n@rmrsk my suggestion would be to pause whilst we wait for confirmation, though @kyleniemeyer has authority on this as TEiC.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3510142661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3510616051","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3510616051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3510616051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7RP7_z","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T10:09:40Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T10:09:40Z","body":"All right -- notify me once we're ready to proceed :)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3510616051/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3511782984","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3511782984","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3511782984,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7RUY5I","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T13:52:54Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T13:52:54Z","body":"Yes, confirmed.\n\n> Finally, allow me to mention once again that almost all parts of the framework will be invoked even by our MAST workflow, from the user configuration and settings, to the complicated portions of multiprocessing and physics method caching and invocation, through timebase interpolations and up to final output.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3511782984/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3554725372","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3554725372","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3554725372,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7T4M38","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-19T21:35:03Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T21:35:03Z","body":"Hi @gtrevisan @LiamPattinson  @jackleland @rmrsk after discussion we will be proceeding with the review so please generate checklists and start working through the repository as you usually would.\n\nPlease complete the review using the open data from MAST.\nIf you encounter issues with data, or in the ability to review the software using open data please raise it here.\n\nI'll check back in a couple of weeks to see how things are progressing, but please tag me with @jatkinson1000 if you have any queries in the meantime.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3554725372/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3558035564","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3558035564","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3558035564,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7UE1Bs","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T13:21:21Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T13:21:21Z","body":":wave: @jatkinson1000, please take a look at the state of the submission (this is an automated reminder).","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3558035564/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3616580399","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3616580399","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3616580399,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7XkKMv","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T11:53:08Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T11:53:08Z","body":"@gtrevisan @jatkinson1000 \n\nI've started my review -- can @gtrevisan comment on the author list? From the documentation at https://mit-psfc.github.io/disruption-py/#credits it looks like there are several other people who should be explicitly listed as authors? ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3616580399/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3616993379","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3616993379","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3616993379,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7XlvBj","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T13:46:26Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T14:17:05Z","body":"Great! Thank you for taking the time.\n\nI have listed as main authors the current MIT PSFC people providing major contributions to the project in terms of effort.\n\nPrevious contributions to the Matlab scripts, currently frozen in the `matlab` branch, are not part of the current package.\nOur non-MIT _temporary_ collaborators who worked on the framework in the past -- very distant past in terms of code -- are credited in the readme and in the commit-centric (not effort-centric) [contribution graph](https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/graphs/contributors).\nThey are also credited, just like most of our other MIT PSFC contributors (either past or present, eg authors of a physics method or two) in the standard-practice team credit -- \"& MIT PSFC Disruptions Group\".\n\nPlease let me know whether this makes sense to you, and as always I'm open to suggestions.\n\n_EDIT: Let me clarify and state the obvious, that is, no difference in credit follows from having an MIT affiliation or not. But we've only had MIT contributors so far, and a couple of MIT-led external temporary collaborators who helped with non-physics-based library work. I believe the Github graph speaks for itself, whereas my choice in the author's list is effort-based with a reasonable cut-off between explicit co-authorship and team co-authorship._","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3616993379/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3626019351","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3626019351","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3626019351,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7YIKoX","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T09:54:16Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T14:16:24Z","body":"Thanks @gtrevisan and @rmrsk \n\nPer the [JOSS guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/review_criteria.html#authorship), the authorship list is for the author to decide, but we ask reviewers to check and share their thoughts as software acquires contribution from many directions. It is not uncommon for something significant to have been missed. At the same time, for long-running software projects it can be hard to get in touch with some of the original notable authors to get their agreement for inclusion.\n\nHowever, it does strike me as odd, based on the commit metrics, that Joshua Lorincz and Herbert Turner are not named.\n\nFurther, even though the MATLAB implementation is no longer used, it appears, based on the README that the new code is a port of this. I, and most others in research software, would argue that ideas and contributions to this code will have had a significant impact on the port and the version that is available today.\n\nAt the end of the day [JOSS leaves it to the author to make the final decision](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/review_criteria.html#authorship), but this is something for you and your collaborators to consider.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3626019351/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3636466411","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3636466411","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3636466411,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7YwBLr","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T10:45:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T14:16:25Z","body":"Hi @LiamPattinson, @jackleland, and @rmrsk \n\nPlease could you let us know how you are progressing with your reviews?\nI see checklists are starting to be filled for all of you, but can't see any linked issues that have been opened.\n\nPlease could you aim to finish working through these over the next week and open any issues for the author to address so that this can continue to progress in a timely manner?\n\n@gtrevisan please reflect on the [JOSS authorship guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/submitting.html#authorship) and whether any of the individuals discussed above have made _\"active [contribution to the] project direction\"_ and confirm when you have reached a decision over authors. It remains your decision, but from my perspective both Herbert and Joshua have made significant contributions to this codebase, including the Python implementation.\n\nI'll check back next Friday, but in the meantime please tag me if you need anything, and place any questions or comments for broader discussion in this thread.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3636466411/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3636467062","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3636467062","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3636467062,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7YwBV2","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T10:46:04Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T10:46:15Z","body":"@editorialbot remind me in 9 days","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3636467062/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3636467185","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3636467185","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3636467185,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7YwBXx","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T10:46:07Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T10:46:07Z","body":"Reminder set for @jatkinson1000 in 7 days","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3636467185/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3636666750","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3636666750","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3636666750,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7YwyF-","user":{"login":"LiamPattinson","id":14332134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMyMTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14332134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson","html_url":"https://github.com/LiamPattinson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T11:36:47Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T11:37:36Z","body":"Hi @jatkinson1000, I made a start yesterday and have a few things to raise -- just getting my thoughts together regarding what should be raised on the repo and what needs to be discussed here.\n\n---\n\nI have managed to run the code on the `slj/mast` branch and can confirm that it works with MAST data:\n\n```console\n$ disruption-py -t mast -o data.csv 28072  # shot chosen at random\n11:09:15.230 [ INFO  ] Starting: disruption_py ~ v0.13.0.dev0 # 6c56dd8c6dc96455eb45076a8151dd4f0037d814 / <username>@<machine>\n11:09:15.230 [ INFO  ] Logging: /tmp/<username>/disruption-py/2025-12-10/11.09.14-gh79suw9/output.log\n11:09:15.230 [WARNING] Cannot import MDSplus, falling back onto mdsthin!\n11:09:15.300 [WARNING] No SQL server/database!\n11:09:15.300 [ INFO  ] Starting workflow: 1 shot / 1 process\n11:09:15.308 [WARNING] No SQL server/database!                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n11:09:28.525 [ INFO  ] #28072 | 0.239s : get_densities                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \n11:09:28.713 [ INFO  ] #28072 | 0.186s : get_ts_parameters                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \n11:09:28.985 [ INFO  ] #28072 | 0.270s : get_gas                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n11:09:29.139 [ INFO  ] #28072 | 0.152s : get_power                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n11:09:30.363 [ INFO  ] #28072 | 1.223s : get_efit_parameters                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n11:09:30.463 [ INFO  ] #28072 | 0.097s : get_ip_parameters                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \n11:09:30.465 [ INFO  ] #28072 | 0.000s : get_ip_parameters                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \n11:09:30.466 [ INFO  ] #28072 | 0.002s : get_time_domain                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n11:09:30.479 [SUCCESS] #28072 | Success! All parameters have data: 23/23 (100.00%) in 2s                                                                                                                                                                                        \n11:09:30.491 [ INFO  ] Completed workflow: retrieved 1/1 shots (100.00%) in 15s (15.191 s/shot)                                                                                                                                                                                 \n11:09:30.504 [ INFO  ] Saved DataFrame in 0.007 s: data.csv\n      shot   time  beta_tor_normal        dip_dt   dipprog_dt         dn_dt  elongation  elongation_axis  greenwald_fraction  ...      n_e_core  outboard_total    power_nbi  power_radiated    t_e_core  time_domain  total_injected  triangularity_lower  triangularity_upper\nidx                                                                                                                           ...                                                                                                                                              \n0    28072  0.200         1.909396 -8.309625e+05  7438.346680  6.530774e+19    2.062146         1.597464            0.300863  ...  2.849903e+19    2.350653e+18  1740606.500    2.553963e+05  913.503906          2.0    8.544779e+20             0.434760             0.450559\n1    28072  0.201         1.911828 -3.332166e+06  7438.446777 -2.237737e+20    2.060759         1.595210            0.298252  ...  2.820074e+19    2.124803e+18  1791835.875    2.564138e+05  924.535767          2.0    8.544802e+20             0.435148             0.450945\n2    28072  0.202         1.914260  3.982028e+06  7363.410156  1.332588e+20    2.059372         1.592956            0.298860  ...  2.790246e+19    1.920654e+18  1799836.625    2.527790e+05  935.567627          2.0    8.544822e+20             0.435536             0.451331\n3    28072  0.203         1.931106 -6.806544e+06  7437.909668 -8.637162e+19    2.043553         1.590004            0.300224  ...  2.791094e+19    1.736121e+18  1788602.875    2.510499e+05  942.691345          2.0    8.544840e+20             0.435916             0.436919\n4    28072  0.204         1.949549  8.232162e+05  7438.010254  2.258102e+19    2.026136         1.586974            0.298432  ...  2.795340e+19    1.569315e+18  1695799.375    2.511199e+05  949.382263          2.0    8.544857e+20             0.436296             0.420868\n..     ...    ...              ...           ...          ...           ...         ...              ...                 ...  ...           ...             ...          ...             ...         ...          ...             ...                  ...                  ...\n244  28072  0.444              NaN  7.631870e+07  7438.482422 -8.753946e+21         NaN              NaN                 NaN  ...           NaN    4.645164e+07  1770374.250    1.574030e+06         NaN          2.0    8.545000e+20                  NaN                  NaN\n245  28072  0.445              NaN -6.085301e+07  7362.715332 -2.105938e+21         NaN              NaN                 NaN  ...           NaN    4.198866e+07  1806915.250    2.705980e+06         NaN          2.0    8.545000e+20                  NaN                  NaN\n246  28072  0.446              NaN -2.837342e+08  7438.683105  5.118323e+19         NaN              NaN                 NaN  ...           NaN    3.795437e+07  1839171.000    4.023606e+06         NaN          2.0    8.545000e+20                  NaN                  NaN\n247  28072  0.447              NaN -3.293859e+08  7438.045410 -5.025239e+21         NaN              NaN                 NaN  ...           NaN    3.430778e+07  1776474.625    4.314760e+06         NaN          2.0    8.545000e+20                  NaN                  NaN\n248  28072  0.448              NaN -2.260863e+08  7438.883301 -2.105232e+21         NaN              NaN                 NaN  ...           NaN    3.101147e+07  1758643.375    3.004428e+06         NaN          2.0    8.545000e+20                  NaN                  NaN\n\n[249 rows x 25 columns]\n```\n\nHowever, I wasn't able to resolve the `No SQL server/database` warnings, and it wasn't clear from the docs how to do so. I was also able to run the tests (after a little tweaking), but there were a lot of failures and I'm currently in the process of sorting which of these are due to an incomplete install and which are due to errors in the code (if any). At a glance, it looks as if the `slj/mast` branch will need some more work before it's production-ready.\n\nFrom the previous discussion regarding access to private data repositories, I believe it's the case that the `slj/mast` branch will need to be merged and a new version will need to be published before I can approve the review -- @jatkinson1000 is this a correct interpretation? If so, I'm happy to continue reviewing from the `slj/mast` branch for now, provided it will be merged at some point in the near future.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3636666750/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3636713368","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3636713368","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3636713368,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Yw9eY","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T11:50:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T11:50:23Z","body":"Thanks @LiamPattinson for that feedback.\n\nYes, the code/version reviewed and published should be identical.\n\n@gtrevisan please confirm if `slj/mast` is to be merged soon and any timescales.\nIt would not be fair to ask reviewers to inspect code/functionality of branches, and then ask them to check again when it is merged. JOSS expects that code comes to review as ready for publication as the author can make it. If there is still development work to be done, including merging of feature branches, then we would need to look at pausing the review whilst this takes place.\nIdeally we'd both want to avoid this as there is no guarantee that reviewers will be available in the future.\n\nRegarding your other points @LiamPattinson - we do not expect you as a reviewer to dedicate significant time to fix failing tests, broken APIs, or unclear install instructions (unless you wish to). The review is intended to check the useability and functionality of the software. Please open these as issues on the repository for the authors to fix, linking back here as described above.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3636713368/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3639011565","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3639011565","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3639011565,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7Y5ujt","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T21:22:21Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T21:22:21Z","body":"That's correct, please continue your reviews on the MAST `slj/mast` branch.\nWe do plan to merge it onto the `dev` branch (our de-facto default branch) in the near future, as soon as we are satisfied with all the framework implications.\nIf JOSS will also require such new MAST-capable `dev` branch to be merged onto `main` and a new v0.13 release to be published on PyPI, I will certainly take care of it at the end of the review process in a timely fashion.\n\nRegarding authors, I have added Amos, Josh, and Bob.\nI am still discussing offline and will report back here when the author list is settled.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3639011565/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3664771069","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3664771069","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3664771069,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7ab_f9","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-17T10:46:09Z","updated_at":"2025-12-17T10:46:09Z","body":":wave: @jatkinson1000, please take a look at the state of the submission (this is an automated reminder).","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3664771069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3666627272","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3666627272","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3666627272,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7ajErI","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-17T18:27:39Z","updated_at":"2025-12-17T18:27:39Z","body":"@jatkinson1000 Just letting you know that I will be late with this review as I am on a short term sick leave. Will try to prioritize this once I feel better...","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3666627272/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3666694328","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3666694328","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3666694328,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7ajVC4","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-17T18:47:54Z","updated_at":"2025-12-17T18:47:54Z","body":"> [@jatkinson1000](https://github.com/jatkinson1000) Just letting you know that I will be late with this review as I am on a short term sick leave. Will try to prioritize this once I feel better...\n\n@rmrsk thanks for updating us and I hope you are doing better soon.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3666694328/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3709815388","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3709815388","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3709815388,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7dH0pc","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T10:20:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T10:20:31Z","body":"Hi @gtrevisan -- I have some comments to the paper itself that should be adressed.\n\n1. I'd like to see the final author list as soon as it is finalized. \n2. The Statement of need section describes DisruptionPy quite well, but does not state its relation to other packages/codes. If other related analysis tools exist, they should be briefly discussed and referenced. If not, a statement on the uniqueness of DisruptionPy would be appropriate.\n3. The references only contain works from the Disruptions Group (Cristina Rea is an author of every referenced paper, except Stillerman 1997). Fusion plasma disruptions is not my field, so for all I know this may or may not be completely appropriate. But at the very least I'd like you to comment as to why there are no references to works outside of the Disruptions Group, and/or make amendments to the list of references if relevant. \n4. The acknowledgement section only mentions the latest funding source, but it seems to me that the software has a longer and perhaps more complicated history? Are there other additional funding sources or projects that should be credited?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3709815388/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3710043565","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3710043565","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3710043565,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7dIsWt","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T11:27:50Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T11:27:50Z","body":"@gtrevisan I also want to echo the issues raised by @LiamPattinson in https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/issues/496, https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/issues/497, https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/issues/498\n\nThe installation instructions are IMO not sufficiently clear, with several errors thrown for private installations (e.g., missing modules mdsthin and MDSplus). \n\nIt would be much more helpful if a straight-line walkthrough of installation and loading of example data was provided (e.g., which example script should be run). For me to continue the review, the issues raised by @LiamPattinson should be adressed first. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3710043565/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3719089734","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3719089734","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3719089734,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7drM5G","user":{"login":"arfon","id":4483,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4483?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon","html_url":"https://github.com/arfon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arfon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T14:16:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T17:25:30Z","body":"👋 This review issue has been updated to reflect JOSS's revised scope policies.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- Documentation links in the reviewer checklist now point to the archived pre-2026 documentation at https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/\n- This ensures the review guidelines match the scope under which this submission was received (this submission is being reviewed by the JOSS criteria before this scope update was made on [5th January 2026](https://blog.joss.theoj.org/2026/01/preparing-joss-for-a-generative-ai-future))\n\n**Important context**\n\nJOSS recently updated its scope to address challenges posed by generative AI (see our [blog post](https://blog.joss.theoj.org/2026/01/preparing-joss-for-a-generative-ai-future) for details). However, **this submission is being reviewed under the previous scope** and should be reviewed according to those guidelines.\n\nThe reviewer documentation that matches the review criteria for this historical submission can be found here: https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/pre-2026-submission/reviewer_guidelines.html\n\nAny questions, please direct them at the editor of this submission. Many thanks!\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3719089734/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3750253759","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3750253759","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3750253759,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7fiFS_","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-14T15:57:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-14T15:57:05Z","body":"@LiamPattinson\nyour 3 issues are resolved.\n\n@rmrsk\nunderstood.\nwrt (1): as we are still developing the MAST branch, we will probably add one or two people down the line.\nwrt (2-3-4): I will start working on some modifications in the paper.\n\nI believe nothing else is preventing you all from continuing the review -- please LMK otherwise. thanks!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3750253759/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3750624590","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3750624590","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3750624590,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7fjf1O","user":{"login":"LiamPattinson","id":14332134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMyMTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14332134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson","html_url":"https://github.com/LiamPattinson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-14T17:09:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-14T17:09:06Z","body":"I'm unsure to what degree this bullet point has been completed:\n\n- [ ] **Example usage**: Do the authors include examples of how to use the software (ideally to solve real-world analysis problems).\n\nThe resources linked in https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/issues/498#issuecomment-3750204544 aren't mentioned in the project itself, and the steps needed to get from the examples in the repo to the data used in the [regression example](https://ai4fusion-wmschool.github.io/summer2025/HandsOn2_Regression_Fusion.html) aren't clear to me, so I don't believe that issue was actually resolved.\n\nOn the other hand, on the `slj/mast` branch, I am now able to run the scripts `examples/defaults.py` and `examples/efit.py`, and I can find descriptions of all of the functions/classes used in the docs, so in that sense there are working examples that demonstrate the core functionality. Whether that's sufficient to fulfil the requirements depends on how much weight the word \"ideally\" is carrying in that bullet point.\n\nIn any case, I believe I'll have to wait until `slj/mast` is merged into `main` before I can tick the box, and it's currently failing a lot of tests for me, so I gather that there's still some work to be done before it'll be ready.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3750624590/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3789054032","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3789054032","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3789054032,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7h2GBQ","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T08:34:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T08:34:22Z","body":"Hi All, I'm back from leave so just checking in on this.\n\nThank you @LiamPattinson, @jackleland, and @rmrsk for your comprehensive reviews and for persevering with evaluating this software.\n\nFrom reading through the comments and issues for this review I am wondering if this software is really in a state where it can be easily reviewed and is easily usable as open-source software by other researchers. Particular points are:\n\n- use of code in an external branch, not the main package as installed from PyPI,\n- various issues with underlying core functionality in databases, dependencies, etc. and\n- lack of clear instructions for installation and usage\n\nas raised by multiple reviewers.\nThis is in addition to other paper-related issues such as protracted authorship debate and reference queries.\n\nIt does not seem to me that these are likely to be resolved in on the timescales expected of a JOSS review\nSee [JOSS Submission requirements](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/submitting.html#submission-requirements)\n> JOSS requires that software should be feature-complete (i.e., no half-baked solutions), [and] packaged appropriately according to common community standards for the programming language being used (e.g., [Python](https://packaging.python.org/), [R](https://r-pkgs.org/index.html))\n\nThere would be no issues with withdrawal and resubmission to JOSS at a later date ([noting that the scope has been updated](https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3719089734)) when all of the the relevant code is in the main branch, installable from PyPI, development has reached a stable point for usability and release, and installation/usage issues have been ironed out. Doing so would be a much more effective use of time for our volunteer reviewers who have already done more here than would usually be expected.\n\nI will not take any action at this moment, but would appreciate if the reviewers could please summarise their thoughts on the above having looked into the software in depth.\n\nRef:\n\n- [JOSS Author Guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/submitting.html#)\n- [JOSS Reviewer Guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/reviewer_guidelines.html)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3789054032/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3789628206","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3789628206","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3789628206,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7h4SMu","user":{"login":"LiamPattinson","id":14332134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMyMTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14332134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson","html_url":"https://github.com/LiamPattinson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T10:46:27Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T10:46:27Z","body":"Thanks @jatkinson1000, I would personally like to see the `slj/mast` branch merged into `main` and a new release to be made before continuing, as without that I'm not able to verify the software's core functionality. I've just checked in on how it's doing, and it looks like it is now passing tests, but I can't say how close it is to being feature-complete.\n\nI think a more detailed worked example or two in the docs would strengthen the project, as while I am able to piece together how things work using the `examples/` scripts and the API docs, there's not a lot to go on as a new user from outside the project. I don't think it would need to be all that complicated; just a light tutorial on how to write a script using `get_shots_data` that pulls some MAST data and then uses it to make a couple of plots relevant to disruptions. It would be useful if it could explain what each of the inputs are and what options are available, especially for things like `RetrievalSettings` which is a bit mysterious to me.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3789628206/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3798496365","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3798496365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3798496365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7iaHRt","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T08:53:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T08:53:35Z","body":"Hi @jatkinson1000 - I just want to touch base and let you know that I share Liam's opinion on this one. I'd like to see the project finish the development process and paper before I continue my review. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3798496365/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3858609159","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3858609159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3858609159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7l_bQH","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T07:48:59Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T07:48:59Z","body":"Thanks @rmrsk and @LiamPattinson for your feedback, it is very helpful.\n@jackleland did you have any thoughts? I can see you are not as far through the checklist as Robert and Liam.\n\n@gtrevisan before I make a decision on this did you have any comments on the feedback above or timescales for a reviewable code?\n\nI'll look to make a decision on this next week.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3858609159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3858611005","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3858611005","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3858611005,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7l_bs9","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T07:49:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T07:49:16Z","body":"@editorialbot remind me in 5 days","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3858611005/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3858611372","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3858611372","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3858611372,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7l_bys","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T07:49:19Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T07:49:19Z","body":"Reminder set for @jatkinson1000 in 5 days","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3858611372/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3860891682","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3860891682","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3860891682,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7mIIgi","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T14:51:56Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T14:51:56Z","body":"we are almost done with the review of our MAST branch.\nI expect to merge `slj/mast` onto `dev` within the next couple of (business) days -- let's say by next Tue.\n\nI will then take another couple of days to prepare our new release, verify changes, carry out on-premises tests, unleash full-scale database workflows, and finally publish v0.13 -- let's say by next Thu.\n\nin other words, if executing from `slj/mast` or `dev` is undesirable, then rest assured that **all reviewers will be able to continue their evaluation from a new `main` release within the next week**.\n\nthat said, there won't be any publication until you all reviewed and green-lit our code, so our minor finishing touches on the manuscript are going to be tackled last.\nI believe reviewers should be able to do the same, and indeed the \"Software paper\" section in the checklist is placed last.\n\nlet me know whether I missed anything! and feel free to re/open any issue on our repo as needed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3860891682/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3861764745","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3861764745","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3861764745,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7mLdqJ","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T17:40:11Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T17:40:11Z","body":"> in other words, if executing from `slj/mast` or `dev` is undesirable, then rest assured that **all reviewers will be able to continue their evaluation from a new `main` release within the next week**.\n\nGreat! Please tag me when this is done :)\n\n> that said, there won't be any publication until you all reviewed and green-lit our code, so our minor finishing touches on the manuscript are going to be tackled last. I believe reviewers should be able to do the same, and indeed the \"Software paper\" section in the checklist is placed last.\n\nI'd like @jatkinson1000 or @kyleniemeyer to comment on whether or not this is acceptable JOSS review practice. I don't think it's fair to ask reviewers to perform partial reviews, especially since the author list is not finalized.  Personally, I'd like to review the complete submission, including the paper, but I will nonetheless accept the recommendations of the editors.\n\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3861764745/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3861823894","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3861823894","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3861823894,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7mLsGW","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T17:52:14Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T17:56:46Z","body":"Thanks @rmrsk and you are correct to ask.\nJOSS reviewers are reviewing the paper and the software sustainability and functionality. They are NOT developers or source reviewers.\n\n@gtrevisan Please do **not** ask our **_volunteer_** JOSS submission reviewers to be reviewing core development of your code.\n\nAs I said above, JOSS expects software to come to review in a functional and useable state ready for review.\nOne of these expectations is packaging and distribution as appropriate for the project - for Python this would be installation from PyPI or Conda, not a clone and dev install.\n\nThe same is true of the paper - this should also be ready for review at time of submission to JOSS.\n\nBased on your outline above I will ask the reviewers to revisit the software and paper on **Friday the 13th March** (to account for Thursday timezones). If at that time they still feel that there are significant barriers to being able to review it in the manner of a regular JOSS submission I will be suggesting withdrawal and resubmission at a later date.\n\nI will let @kyleniemeyer add any further thoughts as an editor in chief, but we have already given this submission a lot of leeway with the reviewers showing great patience and engagement.\n\nCC @LiamPattinson @jackleland ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3861823894/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3861893024","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3861893024","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3861893024,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7mL8-g","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T18:08:03Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T18:08:03Z","body":"the manuscript has been ready for review since Jul 2025.\nI was referring to the minor comments raised by @rmrsk last month, which are going to be implemented as soon as possible.\nalso, the author list is final from my perspective.\n\nI don't think I've received any other comment on the manuscript from @LiamPattinson or @jackleland at this time.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3861893024/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3882864401","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3882864401","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3882864401,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7nb88R","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T07:49:21Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T07:49:21Z","body":":wave: @jatkinson1000, please take a look at the state of the submission (this is an automated reminder).","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3882864401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3885740697","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3885740697","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3885740697,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7nm7KZ","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T17:02:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:02:55Z","body":"version 0.13 is now officially released:\n- https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/releases/tag/v0.13\n- https://pypi.org/project/disruption-py/\n- https://zenodo.org/records/18612738","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3885740697/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3886707932","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3886707932","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3886707932,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7nqnTc","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T19:52:29Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T19:52:29Z","body":"also, the manuscript is now updated according to @rmrsk's suggestions:\n- https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/tree/glt/joss\n- https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/actions/runs/21919837714/artifacts/5471367339\n\nfurther comments:\n\n> 2. The Statement of need section describes DisruptionPy quite well, but does not state its relation to other packages/codes. If other related analysis tools exist, they should be briefly discussed and referenced. If not, a statement on the uniqueness of DisruptionPy would be appropriate.\n\nwe added references to both TokSearch and DEFUSE, which to our knowledge are the only somewhat similar tools.\n\nhttps://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/blob/695c72d4325cc98453e40cd93fafdf3e7bcb932f/paper.md?plain=1#L65-L71\n\n> 3. The references only contain works from the Disruptions Group (Cristina Rea is an author of every referenced paper, except Stillerman 1997). Fusion plasma disruptions is not my field, so for all I know this may or may not be completely appropriate. But at the very least I'd like you to comment as to why there are no references to works outside of the Disruptions Group, and/or make amendments to the list of references if relevant.\n\nthat was the point of our last sentence:\n\nhttps://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/blob/695c72d4325cc98453e40cd93fafdf3e7bcb932f/paper.md?plain=1#L74\n\nwe expect that further visibility in the community through dissemination at conferences and relevant fora will raise the profile of our tool and facilitate broader adoption, all the more now that we support MAST open workflows.\n\n> 4. The acknowledgement section only mentions the latest funding source, but it seems to me that the software has a longer and perhaps more complicated history? Are there other additional funding sources or projects that should be credited?\n\nwe added our ongoing MIT PSFC MFE award:\n\nhttps://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/blob/695c72d4325cc98453e40cd93fafdf3e7bcb932f/paper.md?plain=1#L78","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3886707932/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3893390483","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3893390483","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3893390483,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7oEGyT","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-12T21:06:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T21:06:20Z","body":"@gtrevisan Fantastic - I'm on PTO next week but will prioritize this the week after","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3893390483/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3971414822","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3971414822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3971414822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7stvsm","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T08:01:51Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T08:01:51Z","body":"@editorialbot generate pdf","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3971414822/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3971421864","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3971421864","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3971421864,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7stxao","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T08:03:51Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T08:03:51Z","body":":point_right::page_facing_up: [Download article proof](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openjournals/joss-papers/joss.09364/joss.09364/10.21105.joss.09364.pdf) :page_facing_up: [View article proof on GitHub](https://github.com/openjournals/joss-papers/blob/joss.09364/joss.09364/10.21105.joss.09364.pdf) :page_facing_up: :point_left:","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3971421864/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3979512787","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3979512787","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3979512787,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7tMovT","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-01T08:48:15Z","updated_at":"2026-03-01T08:48:15Z","body":"@rmrsk, @LiamPattinson, and @jackleland \n\nSince you have now had some time to evaluate at the new release please could you confirm whether the required additions have been made and if you feel it is in a state in which you are able to review it for JOSS?\n\nIf so, I'd like to proceed as close to the proposed JOSS timeline as we can from now, given this has dragged on (through no fault of the reviewers).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3979512787/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3982762595","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3982762595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3982762595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7tZCJj","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T08:01:59Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T09:06:25Z","body":"@jatkinson1000 @gtrevisan Yeah, I only have some minor comments at this point.\n\n1. The paper looks all right, but I'd suggest refactoring the summary section. Presently, it doesn't actually describe the high-level functionality of the software, as required by the JOSS guidelines. See https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/paper.html#what-should-my-paper-contain. I suggest moving the present summary into the statement of need section, and moving paragraph 1 & 3 from the statement section into the summary. \n\n2. The automated tests are all live tests that connect to servers with secret tokens. Is there any way the tests can be verified locally?\n\n3. Consider including pytest as a dependency, as examples/efit.py relies on it.\n\nFinally, these two points can be improved:\n\n<img width=\"780\" height=\"102\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/32362f77-901b-4785-933e-3b6b4f2afc76\" />\n\nThe current examples seem comparatively shallow, and could be extended to \"solve real-world analysis problems\". Internal Python functions have proper docstrings, but some of the functionality requires users to dig through the source code. It would be beneficial - although not mandatory - to build a full Python API documentation. \n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3982762595/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3984731442","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3984731442","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3984731442,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7tgi0y","user":{"login":"LiamPattinson","id":14332134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMyMTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14332134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson","html_url":"https://github.com/LiamPattinson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T14:26:39Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T14:26:39Z","body":"@jatkinson1000 I haven't yet had a chance to go over everything again, but I've scheduled some time tomorrow afternoon.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3984731442/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3986163114","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3986163114","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3986163114,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7tmAWq","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T18:37:26Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T18:37:26Z","body":"@rmrsk quick reply to part of your questions.\n\n2. as discussed, [all machines apart from MAST](https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py?tab=readme-ov-file#devices) require authentication.\n tests are trivial for any user if ran from those on-premise computers, but do require opening tunnels otherwise.\n in the spirit of CI/CD, I've set up remote testing to allow me to verify our workflows for all machines in parallel at every commit/PR.\n in any case, you are welcome to run tests for MAST locally -- please see below.\n\n3. `pytest` is indeed a dependency [in the `dev` group](https://github.com/MIT-PSFC/disruption-py/blob/c0c9242183a09f124fb94e14f904552a38265781/pyproject.toml#L6-L14).\n tests or examples are not part of the PyPI release, as usual, but they are part of the repo and are useful starting points for users/developers -- please see below.\n\n- **functionality documentation**: the docstrings for each physics method are already parsed and offered as an easily-browsable dynamically-generated webpage -- is this what you would like to see?\n https://mit-psfc.github.io/disruption-py/usage/physics_methods/mast_method_reference/#disruption_py.machine.mast.physics.MastPhysicsMethods.get_densities\n please correct me if I misunderstood.\n\n### test execution\n\nif someone clones our repo, local tests are as easy as:\n```\nmake install test-fast test\n```\nwhich is equivalent to:\n```bash\n# install with dev deps\npoetry install --with dev\n\n# run fast tests\nGITHUB_ACTIONS=true poetry run pytest -v tests\n\n# run full tests\npoetry run pytest -v tests\n```\nor any other command to a similar effect, eg:\n```\nuv sync --group dev\nuv run pytest\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3986163114/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3989170802","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3989170802","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3989170802,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7txepy","user":{"login":"rmrsk","id":39047996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDQ3OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39047996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk","html_url":"https://github.com/rmrsk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmrsk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T07:15:25Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T07:15:25Z","body":"@gtrevisan Thanks for answering that right away!\n\nOk, I was able to run all the tests locally as well, so consider that box ticked. For the documentation, I was referring to some files that could not be found in the webpages, particularly some of those that lie under disruption_py/core. Since this doesn't mean anything substantial for the review, I will tick this box anyways. If these files were left out of the generated documentation by accident, at least you now know about it...\n\nThe only major item left on my list is the improvement on the Summary section, which should be a quick fix. A better example that provides a bit more depth than the current ones would be beneficial, but not a mandatory requirement according to JOSS guidelines. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3989170802/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3989280218","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3989280218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3989280218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7tx5Xa","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T07:39:17Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T07:39:17Z","body":"Glad to see this is progressing, just a note @gtrevisan to say that if @rmrsk needed to ask for these instructions they need providing clearly as part of the documentation, not just on this thread, before the box can truly be ticked.\nAssuming they're not already there and @rmrsk just missed them I'd suggest opening an issue (linking back to this review) to log this.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3989280218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3992412885","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-3992412885","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":3992412885,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7t92LV","user":{"login":"LiamPattinson","id":14332134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMyMTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14332134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson","html_url":"https://github.com/LiamPattinson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T17:09:11Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T17:09:11Z","body":"I've ticked all but two points on my list, with the remaining work being this point raised by @rmrsk:\n\n> The paper looks all right, but I'd suggest refactoring the summary section. Presently, it doesn't actually describe the high-level functionality of the software, as required by the JOSS guidelines. See https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/paper.html#what-should-my-paper-contain. I suggest moving the present summary into the statement of need section, and moving paragraph 1 & 3 from the statement section into the summary.\n\nI agree that the summary paragraph would be better suited in the statement of need, and that the functionality of the software should be described in the summary, but otherwise the paper itself looks good to me.\n\nI was able to get the tests to run just fine using `uv`, but was also a little surprised to see `pytest` wasn't installed by `uv sync`. I'd normally expect the `dev` group to be switched on by default and for `uv sync --no-dev` to be necessary if users want to skip it. It might be worth mentioning in the README that developers should run `uv sync --group=dev` to help out those who aren't so familiar with this stuff, but that's a _very_ minor point.\n\nAs stated before, I would personally like to see a more in-depth example/tutorial, but I was able to test the basics of the software from the README alone, and I can piece together how to do more complicated things by looking at the `examples/` directory and the API docs, so I'll consider that box ticked.\n\nIn summary, beyond the issue with the paper, all looks ready to me.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3992412885/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4011648640","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-4011648640","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":4011648640,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7vHOaA","user":{"login":"jatkinson1000","id":109271713,"node_id":"U_kgDOBoNaoQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109271713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000","html_url":"https://github.com/jatkinson1000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jatkinson1000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T13:07:00Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T13:07:00Z","body":"Thanks reviewers.\n\n@gtrevisan please could you look at making the requested changes to the paper and addressing the other above points over the next week, thanks.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4011648640/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4011814561","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-4011814561","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":4011814561,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7vH26h","user":{"login":"gtrevisan","id":20228269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI4MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20228269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan","html_url":"https://github.com/gtrevisan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtrevisan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T13:39:16Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T13:39:16Z","body":"@rmrsk @LiamPattinson\nI think my latest addition to the readme (#525) satisfies your comments about dev/deps, but please let me know otherwise.\n\n@jatkinson1000 \nI already adjusted the paper, but I am currently waiting for coauthors' approval, so I will push the final version into the JOSS branch early next week at the latest.\nalso, we still haven't heard back from @jackleland...","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4011814561/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4012582114","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364#issuecomment-4012582114","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/9364","id":4012582114,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7vKyTi","user":{"login":"LiamPattinson","id":14332134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMyMTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14332134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson","html_url":"https://github.com/LiamPattinson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiamPattinson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T16:00:40Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T16:00:40Z","body":"Thanks @gtrevisan, the changes look good to me. I'll take another look at the paper once it's ready.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4012582114/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused"